{
 "schema": 1,
 "title": "RayCAD thread standards",
 "generatedBy": "tools/gen_thread_table.py",
 "units": "Lengths in mm; unified sizes also give inches in the fields ending in In.",
 "method": {
  "profile": "ISO 68-1 / ASME B1.1 basic 60 degree profile: H = sqrt(3)/2 P; the basic internal thread depth is 5/8 H on each side.",
  "basicMinorDiameter": "D1 = D - 2 x 5/8 H = D - 1.082532 P.",
  "tapDrillMetric": "d = D - P (about 75 % thread), rounded to the nearest point of a grid of 0.05 mm below 3 mm, 0.1 mm from 3 mm to below 14 mm, 0.25 mm from 14 mm to 25 mm and 0.5 mm above 25 mm; a value half way between two points takes the larger.",
  "tapDrillUnified": "d = D - 0.974279 P = D - 0.75 x 2 x 3/4 H: the '75 % thread' of the percentage-of-thread rule (which counts 3/4 H = 0.649519 P per side as full depth), rounded to the nearest of the number gauge drills #1 to #80, the letter gauge drills A to Z and fractional drills in 1/64 in steps; a tie would take the larger drill (none occurs in this table).",
  "note": "Generated values. A shop chart may pick a drill one step away (for example 10.2 mm for M12x1.75, where this rule gives 10.3 mm); check the material and the thread class before tapping."
 },
